X-Deja-AN: 348897358
References: <3547941D.CDB4B8C4@lgcy.com>
Organization: Malaspina University-College
Newsgroups: comp.periphs.scsi,comp.sys.dec


In article <3547941D.CDB4B8C4@lgcy.com>, 
   Candace Hsiao <hsiao@lgcy.com> writes:

> Just got ahold of a number of Digital DSP5400S 4GB drives. Don't,
> however, have the jumper settings, and can't get them (Digital says
> Quantum, Quantum says "duh?")...
> 
> Does anyone out there know which jumper terminates/unterminates these
> beasts?
> 

   You need a jumper between pins 17 and 18 of the option connector,
where the numbers go as follows:


     +--------------------------
     |21                      1|
     |                         |
     |22                      2|
     +__________________________
           Electronics module


   So 17 and 18 would be the 3rd column from the left. If the drive
is a 5400W ( wide variant ) the jumper would go on pins 19-20 instead
of 17-18.

    Address selection goes on pins 5-6, 3-4 and 1-2 of this connector
(where 5-6 are the MSB and 1-2 are the LSB)

