The original table ( below ) is not valid since it compares SGI local
node latency ( and not the latency to any memory location in the system
) to the latency for any memory location for the DEC, SUN, and HP
uniform memory access SMPs. It is like comparing apples to bananas. It
makes more sense to compare the average latency in the above table to
the DEC, HP, and SUN numbers below. In addition, the SPECfp numbers for
the SGI were generated by running in the local node memory - an
application that was big enough to require the memory of other nodes
will, of course, suffer because of the decrease in memory performance
once you go "off node" - memory performance on the uniform memory access
SMP is constant ( by definition ). All of this stuff doesnt really
matter since the performance and functionality of the systems for your
workload is more important.


