I'm not a hardware engineer and I've never been let loose anywhere near any
kind of VAX 7000 series system, so take what I say with a pinch of salt.

But that's never stopped me before so here goes ...

For 5 or six CPU systems you are supposed to use E2045-AB. But an -AA 07 is the
same etch as an -AB so your 07 rev boards will possibly be OK. Your 06 boards
are probably not OK and may need to be swapped.

I presume that you can get some sort of trade-in to take your two rev S06
boards to E2045-AB (I don't know the latest rev for that module).

When you enquire about the trade-in you might want to check that the above
is anywhere near the truth ...!


Antonio


