I'd *love* to see SAP run on a VMS-based Alpha system in a cluster.  I
have seen many Oracle applications on VMSclusters and they literally
scream.  The OS handles the locking, and the application only needs to
worry about locks if it wants to do special processing (ie, rather
than just wait for the lock to be released).  This can be transparent
to the application, though a software package written to a
sufficiently-low level of the OS may need to implement it's own lock
handling algorithms.  The message passing for distributed lock
management is handled by the OS, so all applications tend to behave
predictably.

