It must be a TK50 I do not think the "DLT" was made until 1994-5(maybe even
later).  So anything made before that time would be the infamous TKXX stuff.
The TK50/70 came in a cumbersome shoebox and had two scsi connectors that
faced downwards under a carrying handle.  Oooh yeah it it is a beige box
with a folding handle on the rear it most likely is an old TK tape
subsystem.  They made some SCSI variants (not true SCSI) for the Vax and DEC
stations of the time.  this has a little piggyback board on top of a real TK
drive that converts TK-SCSI and back.  The Sense command of any modern SCSI
controller is really confused by the reply and the old VAX/DEC stations were
confused by any modern SCSI tape unit, they had fixed firmware and expected
a certain tape (TKXX) to show up.

