References: <353F7847.41C6@phy.ucsf.edu>
Organization: Canadian Institute for Theoretical Astrophysics
Reply-To: mark@cita.utoronto.ca
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


[ Gaylord Holder ]

>>  I recently installed an RZ28 from an Alphastation 500 into an Alpha
>>  433au.  The disk kept spinning down about every 40 minutes or so.  There
>>  were no problems getting the disk to spin up.  I had the same problem
>>  with an IBM disk on a Alpha500au.
>>
>>  I couldn't find any way to configure the drives to do this in the
>>  installation manuals.  Can anyone suggest what might be going on?

Yep.  Power-save mode.  Rather silly, it seems to me (I mean, how much of a
saving is there, really?), and totally stupid to make it the default rather
than providing it as an option.

You can disable this misfeature by using "dxpower" (or "dxkerneltuner -power",
which is all that "dxpower" does).  Or, you might find it easier just to edit
/etc/sysconfigtab, appending ...

pwrmgr:
	disk_spindown=0

... and rebooting.

