of what convinces me of of the superiority of Digital Unix. But I just
don't find
it appropriate to do in a public forum.

In truth, Andrew, is it possible that you're starting to see a little
handwriting on
the wall, and you don't like the message? I know if I were in your
shoes, I'd be afraid.
Very afraid. The tide of public opinion can be an unreasoning
juggernaut, as Digital found
out when UNIX started to undermine VMS sales. I think that juggernaut is
about to turn
on Sun, and I sort of doubt that they can get out of the way fast
enough.

