format and `silly password database', too.

And as far as `no Mach ancestry' goes, remember that 4.3's ``machine
independent'' VM subsystem is a vax pagetable with vax ptes.  So
either you emulate a vax pagetable, like I'm told early SunOS did (not
quite so disgusting, I guess, with TLB miss-handling in software); or
you roll your own VM subsystem.


