Yes, especially if you're comparing to 1.2 or 1.2.1. Eek, those didnt
even have shared libraries.  

And another point to note; its hardly fair to compare GCC-compiled
NetbSD kernels to Ultrix kernels compiled with the mipsco compiler.
That'll get you 10%-15% right there.  NetBSD/pmax has all the hooks to
compile with the mipsco suite (that's how the first kernels were
bootstrapped), and all the hooks are definitely there, but they
haven't been used and may have rusted.

That might make a fun project if you wanted to take it on :).


