Stephen.

The 1st question is what O/S do you want to run  - if NT/Dec Unix/Linux
you've got more choice but if you want to run OpenVMS (license permitting),
you will be spending more.

Next question is what performance are you looking for, range from 133 to
600Mhz.

NT Only,

There is a company in Holland that can supply XL 300/266 systems at a
reasonable cost.
Could by AXP133pci motherboard, which are relatively cheap but 133Mhz? can
add on industry standard peripherals.

NT or DEC Unix

Quite some choice but I have found suppliers only want to sell you 533Mhz +,
best price quoted:-
Alpha SX motherboard with 533Mhz processor = �750 (+VAT).
Alpha LX motherboard (more CPU cache) with 533Mhz processor = �1500 (+VAT).
There are a number of Suppliers - Samsung UK, Prolinx (supply Aspen Alpha
motherboards US) who will sell motherboards but limited choice - high cost.

NT/Unix & OpenVMS.

Really your looking at buying second-user DEC systems, from approx �1500 for
basic system - DEC3000-300 166Mhz, 1Gb.

I have been attempting to build a system for the last couple of months and
found it very difficult to get a deal on alpha motherboard/peripherals.

If you find any good offers be sure to let me know.

Keith Madge





