profession. However, the entire story has one big problem, its
content is largely irrelevant to the typical corporate customer.
They simply don't care about standard performance numbers.
They have some performance requirements for which they
want to have some guarantees that they are met. Sometimes
they ask for standard numbers  but in a entire evaluation process it's not more
than a tiny fraction of the deal. So our little war might at best
be amusing for some folks on the list, for most probably boring
and certainly for decision makers mostly irrelevant (if they even
happen to read usenet)
