Actually we had to go through the same thing here.  The export program in SAS that
you are refering to has a "LIBRARY" command which can create that interim file
format you were referring to in order to export an entire directory.  The reason
for this is a move from a 32-bit to 64-bit OS.  The SunOS SAS datasets should have
a .ssd01 extension and when imported to DU they should be .ssd04

We also tried to find a global fix but it just doesn't exist.

Ed Notari

