If this unit has the keyboard, enter setup mode (Ctrl/Setup) so the
setup light blinks. Then print out the current settings with the
status button (8?). This should give you a list of settings next to
letters.  Find the baud rate setting (a?) and enter it at the keyboard
followed by the equal; sign and a question mark (a=?).  This should
print out a list of options for that setting. Then just enter
setting=value (a=n for 9600). I bel;eive to save the setting is either
shift/9 or shift/s.

If this unit does not have the keyboard, the settings are made via the
2 switch packs under the carraige.

NOTE:  This is completely from memory. Take it for what it's worth.

Steve

