One of out Alpha 3000-600's died over the weekend. On 
Saturday morning the poor thing was sitting there repeatedly
cycling through the initial stages of the boot process. It would
get as far as starting to load vmunix, then barf (without error
messages) and start the whole boot process over again. Switching
the machine off and then back on again made the problem worse. 
Now nothing happens, no messages on the screen. The post power-up
LED's get as far as having 7 through 4 lit, the others remaining
blank. 

We've tried obvious things such as swapping out power supplies
etc., but it seems to be a mother-board problem. The question
is, what to do with the machine? We could salvage the hard drive
and memory but it would also be nice to get it fixed. The problem
with that is the cost that Digital charges for just looking at 
the thing means we might as well buy a new one. Has anyone
had any good experiences with third party groups who can reliably
fix an Alpha at a reasonable cost?

Many thanks for your help,

Adrian
 


