Andrew Harrison SUNUK Consultancy <andrew.harrison@uk.sun.com#> writes:
> Pardon me for asking but why do you need >4GB address space fora web server. They
> generally use UFS and the UFS buffer cache
> can be as big as you want it to be.
--

Actually, that's a design flaw introduced by the use of machines
without support for large memory. Typically, the proxy server would
want to manage the memory space themselves. If nothing else, the
problem is that the UFS is a system-call away, and that the
concurrency controls on the UFS pool may be more restrictive than the
proxy server needs.


-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



