I'm having a strange problem with my modem. Is there anybody with a
solution?
My setup is as follows:
Computer (laptop): Digital HiNote VP500 series (probably the VP567
model,
there is no indication on the computer), 133MHz w. MMX, 1.4Gb, 16Mb,
CD-rom, 2 PCMCIA-ports
Modem: Xircom CreditCard Ethernet+Modem 28.8
Telephone: Tone

I'm using these programs:
Windows '95, 4.00 950B
Phoenix CardServices and Enumerator (Cardagnt 3-4-97 23.54) with the
Upgrade95 (29-9-97 10.53). (this gives me 2 X 'Cirrus Logic 6832
PCMCIA/Cardbus' and 1 x 'Phoenix CardServices and Enumerator' in
configuration/system/PCMCIA-socket)

The problem:

The modem will not dial ('there is no dialtone'), when I try to connect
to
my provider. It will however send a fax correctly, using Micosoft Fax.
It
also will dial a number, when I give instructions manually in
Hyperterminal
(for instance: atdt 123456).

On the basis of my modemlogfie the helpdesk of my provider thinks that
the
different commands for the modem come to fast and that either the modem
or
the PCMCIA cardprogram (Cardagnt) has problems with this. When typing
instructions manually, this obviously is no problem (my typing is not
that
fast!).

What have I tried?

-The modem works fine on another laptop (not a Digital).
-Another (external, serial port) modem works fine on my computer. I have

not yet tried another PCMCIA modem on my computer, because nobody I know

has one. I think of trying a shop to lend me one.
-Deleting the windows directory and reinstalling Windows '95 makes no
difference.
-Deleting Cardagnt leaves the PCMCIA ports undetected. In the bios
there's
no reference to the PCMCIA port, so I think I'll have to use Cardagnt.
-Without the upgrade95 for Cardagnt there are a lot of problems with the

ethernet part of the card and my soundcard. With the upgrade95 these
problems are over and the ethernet connection works fine.
-I did not use the modem and ethernet at the same time, because I know
that
will cause problems.
-I tried different cables to the 'telephone-wallplug' and I tried
everything somewhere else: no go.
-Tired of it all, I tried selling the modem, but even that didn't work!

Here is a session of my modemlogfile. Perhaps somebody can tell me if
the
helpdesk is right in its diagnose. Perhaps somebody has a brilliant
solution, anything! I want on the net!

Nico, Amsterdam

