In article <3534AD1F.25FD75CA@cpmx.saic.com>, bb1@mail.tomco.net writes:
>Has anyone had to remove NT4.0 from an Alpha 2100 so that UNIX can be
>re-installed?  I can find no documentation on this task.

Reboot:
  select "Supplementary menu"  (quickly, or it will boot WNT again)
  select "Set up the system"
  select "Switch to OpenVMS or Unix console"

I think it reboots at that point (I have not done this in a while).  You'll
come up in the SRM console.  Uh, I think the time will be wrong, so reset
that. Then reinstall DU. 

