	Hi, folks!

	If you had problems with CPU load under Win95 on your laptop and
tried all Power Management features in your BIOS and Windows settings, without
any result - then try CPUidle program. I had a very nasty perfomance of my
Digital HiNoteVP ( with P120 in 15 minutes it was performing Wintune tests
as 486-66!) , I upgraded CPU to P166MMX and then it was working as P75!
But after installing that program everything works just perfectly! Even with
more power emission of new CPU. The matter of fact is that when your system
do nothing , Win95 issues NOP commands to your CPU which heats it so as if
it was working on some program, and  CPUidle intercepts from Win95
such moments and issues to CPU another instruction - HLT (Halt), which
completely stops CPU, letting him to cool down.

	If you are interested check the site :

	http://www.stud.uni-hannover.de/~goetz

Another interesting issue I found is new technology chip cooler
based on Petlier effect. It is a semiconductor slim element (like
sandwich ) which pumps out the heat out of one surfice and passes it
to another. Just imagine up to 128W of instant heat pumped off !!!!
First time I read about it @ http://www.abit.com
                                               in section "Accessories".


	If you plan to speed up your system by changing external bus
frequency this may be a good investment to prevent CPU from being overheated.


	Regards

P.S. Any succesfull experiments regarding impovement of your laptop
productivity
     are welcome.











