The K6-200 uses a 2.9v regulator and there is not a regulator for the
Venturis 5xxx systems that will supply that voltage. You might be able to
get an upgrade kit that contains a regulator (I've heard of something called
the "Evergreen" kit that is a K6-200 on a small pcb that plugs into the
socket7. Check your motherboard, some Veturis systems has a socket 5 and
some had a socket 7. It makes a difference for upgrading. Also, you probably
need the latest BIOS if you plan on using one of the Intel OverDrive chips.
The latest BIOS for Venturis 5xxx is 2.03 and will be available from
Digital's WEB site by 22-Apr-98 (2.02 is currently available):

http://www.windows.digital.com

Look in the Drivers section, then select the Intel x86 section.

