sam@upcl.univ-lyon1.fr (Samuel):
> How change a RZ23L-E from Master configuration to Slave configuartion.

In my vocabulary, a RZxx drive is a SCSI device.  SCSI devices don't
have "masters" or "slaves" but IDs ranging from 0-7 or 0-15 on newer
"wide SCSI" buses.  SCSI IDs are not priviledged over other IDs.  On
a SCSI bus there is only the controller leading the others but there
can be any ID assigned to the controller (7 is the usual one, on the
DS2100 it's 6 and the Indigo at work uses 0, which confused my quite
a lot when setting it up the first time).

Maybe you're thinking of a RX23 floppy disk drive ?  Floppy disks do
have IDs (originally there could have been 4 but the IBM PC crippled 
the system to two by using only ID0 and addressing the drives with a
cable midification).

Greetings,
