bb1@mail.tomco.net wrote:
> 
> Has anyone had to remove NT4.0 from an Alpha 2100 so that UNIX can be
> re-installed?  I can find no documentation on this task.
> 
> Please help!

Very simple. The 2100 like most alpha servers except in some sense the
8000 series have both arc (NT ) and srm (VMS+UNIX) firmware at all
times.
	If you are in arc (eg running NT) go though the config
menu and select the switch console to other OS and choose Digital UNIX
or VMS both seem to work and are the same execpt OS_TYPE is different
the both have the >>> console prompt.

then power cycle the machine as it says to do. Then after the init
you should see the >>> srm prompt. to get back to arc type arc
at the >>> prompt. Somethings eg ecu only run from the arc so you
always have them both. There are are few brain damaged alphas that
only have arc and no srm - the 2100 is not one of them.

show dev and pick the cdrom drive RRDxx device which should be dka600
or dka400
put the Digital UNIX cdrom in the drive and boot dka600 and
away you go. Don't forget to upgrade the firmware and then run
ecu when you finish which of course will take you back via the 
arc to do that.


	Cheers
		Mark :)



