I got a phone call last week from a guy in another department asking
me for help with one of their systems.  It tunrs out that this is a
Sun 3/75 or Sun 3/160 (this according to the boot-up screen banner).
There is a dual ribbon cable coming out of the back of the Sun cabinet
and going to another box that is some sort of scanner for reading and
storing x-ray films.  In looking through the documentation, there is
a LSI-11 (something) with a DR-11 running the film scanner.

When I boot the system, it finds the disk drive, mounts it, etc. but
seems to have problems with the film scanner.  It seems to hang a long
time on scanning the SCSI bus, but then again that might be because of
the external optical drives(?). At the end of this, it dismounts the
disk and says to repair the disk manually and then restart with
/etc/something.  One of things I need to have Frank do is put in an
optical disk and try rebooting.

According to Frank, one day it just wouldn't boot, so it doesn't sound
like a disk has to be in there.  It's not clear if the DR-11 in the
scanner isn't responding, if the Sun equipment is having a problem or
if the LSI is out to lunch.  The optical drives are powered on, but
I'm not sure if there is anything in them.

BTW, they first called the company that sold it to us and asked for help.
