: Who is employed by NONE OF THE ABOVE

I disagree with which ones the market will coalesce around.  And I 
seriously doubt SCO will be one of them.  My tendency is to expect
the dominant players of today to continue to be dominant.  The two
that I am reasonably sure will be around are Solaris and AIX.  The
other one I would expect to survive is HPUX.  DUNIX might remain
viable.  SCO will be marginalized, having little to no
consistent support from any major hardware vendor.  IRIX will
also fade away, as it seems today that they are spinning off MIPS
and don't have any major CPUs in the pipeline.  I suspect they
might be snapped up by some other company who'll want access
to their NUMA and graphics hardware designs.  I just don't see
them surviving as a Wintel vendor.









