Hi Megan,

The mono monitor is the VR201, the same monitor (and cable) used on the Rainbow, Decmate II,
Pro 3XX, etc.  The VR241 color monitor should also work, but there were at least two different
cables for it - "I think" one cable was for the DEC PC family ... Rainbow, Decmate, Pro,
and the other cable was for the VT-240 or Micro Vax applications.

The keyboard is the LK201 again from the Rainbow, Decmate, Pro series or from any of the
DEC terminals VT220, 320, etc.


As far as operating system DEC only supported the WPS word processing on the DECmate II and 
III, but maybe someone was able to hack something up and get OS/8 to run on it.

If you hear of anyone that has OS/8 running on DECMATE II or III, I would love to hear about
it, I have an application that a customer is running from paper tape on an 8E that I would
try and convert to the DECmate.  I could of course add an RX01 or RX02 to the PDP8E, but
they are far away and I don't want to travel there to maintain the PDP8 anymore, with 
DECmates they could just ship me the unit to repair, or I could just send them a spare.


Jim Gonzalez
 

