In article <6gm3mj$o35@charity.ucr.edu>,
Chris Ulrich <insom@math.ucr.edu> wrote:
>In article <6gl2pp$oh4$2@plug.news.pipex.net>,
>Laurence Blunt <xtj12@dial.pipex.com> wrote:
>>faster than Alpha that would mean the end. However Merced is expected to be
>>about 1/3 the performance of current Alpha systems when it appears, it is
>>also going to cost more, due to Merced being 40% bigger than the 21264.
>>Laurence Blunt.
>
>  From the spec.org web pages, the current fastest alpha, an AlphaServer
>4100 5/600, as tested in Oct-97 (available Apr-98) has a SPECint95 of 18.8
>and a SPECfp95 of 51.4.

This is really a misuse of the SPECfp95 benchmark.  You're comparing
apples and oranges.  The 4100 5/600 SPECfp95 number you cite, 51.4, is for
a system with 4 CPU's.  It's not really fair to compare 4 CPU's to
one.

The 21264 will (it is claimed) get a single-CPU performance in the 
range of 50-70, which I hope is what Mr. Blunt was talking about when 
he claimed that "current alphas" are 3x faster than Merced will be.
I also hope he meant "floating point performance".

I'm not familiar with what the performance claim for Merced on introduction
is.

>  BTW: is the AlphAserver 5/600 shipping?  How much does it cost?  Also,

As far as I know, it is.  Prices are in the 100k range for these systems
(reasonably configured.)

A more comparable machine to the 333MHz P-II from DEC's line is
the PC164SX/533, which gets:
SPECint95:  12.4
SPECfp95:  16.1

>why is it that the AlphaServer 8400 5/625 with a 612 MHz 21164 is a tiny

I think the memory subsystem on the DEC 4100 is better somehow.  Either
the cache is faster, bigger, or the memory bus is better.  I am not
very sure of this.

>bit slower than the 600mhz 21164 in the 5/600?  The only difference is
>the 8mb vs 4mb 3rd level cache.  Interestingly, the PII has no 3rd level
>cache at all...

The top two levels of cache on the 21164A processor are "onchip".
The PII has L1-on-chip cache and L2-off chip cache.

The 21164 Alpha has both 16k-L1 and 96k-L2 on chip:  the 3rd level
caches are offchip.

PeterM




