> I have a VaxSERVER (NOT a VAXStation -- this is definitely a
>VaxSERVER) 3100 system that I could really use some hardware info on.


A VAXServer 3100 is a MicroVAX 3100. The only different thing is that it is
limited to ONE use (OPA0:) and has different VMS License Requirements (B
instead of C). A Workstation (VAXStation) requires Type D.

Please refere to:

http://www.digital.com/info/QB0009/QB0009MW.DOC

about connection external devices.

