Bill Bradford wrote:
> 
> I'm looking for an RRD40 or VAXstation-compatible external CD-ROM
> drive; I need something that I can use to boot a VAXstation 3100 with
> the hobbyist VMS CD-ROM.

Hi Bill,

Actually, I've successfully used a standard Toshiba SCSI CD-ROM, and
just about any generic CD-ROM _should_ be able to boot the Hobbyist
CD-ROM.

The trick is that the CD-ROM must have Parity Enabled.  There should
be a jumper setting on any standard SCSI CD-ROM that enables parity.
If it's not enabled, you probably won't be able to boot from it or
see it.  Or you might -- SCSI is weird that way :)


-Seth



