:Here is what its going to do:
:
:Web Server (small webserver....)
:Sendmail Server
:POP3 Server
:INN Server (however currently we aren't even filling up 4 gigs, so don't
:start telling me I need 4x9 gig drives like three others have)
:RADIUS server (for ascend dialins...)

:I definately want something expandable.... it doesn't have to be really
:really expandable... we operate in a small town community, and we
:definately don't need something huge.  Our upsteam provider who is in the
:same community as us has about 1,000 customers and are doing fine on a DEC
:AlphaServer 1000 4/266 with 96 megs of RAM and a hefty newsfeed.

  Most current Alpha CPUs are at least that fast, if not faster.

  I would not skimp on the memory configured -- Alpha and other
  RISC systems like having memory -- I'd treat 64 to 96 MB as a
  starting point, and would work upward from there.  Insufficient
  physical memory is among the most common of the typical system
  performance impediments.

:Here is about what I want:
:
:I'm still torn between the AlphaServers, and the AlphaStations..
:
:266 MHz - 400 MHz Processor (I'm not so sure I need a 400 MHz machine)
:96 - 128 megs of RAM
:DISK space... the biggey... here is what my providers server has:
:
:1 RZ29B
:1 RZ28B

  By current standards, these are moderate-sized disks.

:1 RRD45 (CD-ROM?)

  Correct.

:1 TLZ07 (tape?)

  Correct.  Specifically a DAT.

:2 meg PCI video card
:As far as a monitor a 15" is fine.
:
