> are connected to bus, data transfer is ok, there are no errors.
> I am using DU 3.2G with latest patches.
> Does anybody know solution of my problem????
> 
> Greetz Pawel.
---
The golden rule of the SCSI bus is that any cable is too long.

Keep SCSI interconnecting cables as short as possible, and ensure that
the drives you added are not adding multiple terminations, and that
you've got the bus terminated correctly.



