peripherals, including an old 5 meg removable platter "hard drive." He
wants to be paid money for these things, no doubt owing to his being one
of those TANSTAAFL liberty-minded individualists.

When I suggested that the market for such equipment (acquired by his
vendor in October 1979 and by him in December 1979) might be limited, he
