Shannon Knows DEC's Digital Doggerel

(c) 1998 by Terry C. Shannon


Presented for your viewing pleasure are several out-takes from the
Digital
Dog column in the April 2, 1998 issue of Shannon Knows DEC , The
Newsletter
That Takes No Prisoners. Suffice it to say that these timely tidbits
offer
Conclusive Proof of Canine Clairvoyance. 

Enjoy,

Terry C. Shannon, Publisher
http://www.acersoft.com

He's baaaack! Yes, the Snoop With a Thousand Livers, a.k.a. DEC's worst
nightmare, has turned up like the proverbial bad penny in IS/IT
BackOffice
Magazine . No longer content to foster heartburn in the ranks of the DEC
Product Police, Charlie Matco is taking aim at the Borg of Bellevue! And
to
think that Bill Gates believed that his biggest problem was Belgian
creme
pies!

Columbia, SC-based KryoTech, Inc. again demoed its 767MHz Alpha
EV56 box at the WNT Wizards Symposium, proving that off-the-shelf
components can boost the speed of a stock Alpha workstation by 30
percent
or more. SKD expects that this wizardry will be available to mere 
mortals in very short order. More info is at http://www.kryotech.com.

Digital still won't disclose the magnitude of the Alpha base, but
sources
confirm SKD's "North of 400K systems" estimate. And a recent letter from
Bob Robert Palmer indicated that 27 percent, or 17,592, of the CPUs in
the
world's fastest computers are Alphas. What Palmer failed to mention is
that
the announcement of another fab partner is imminent. SKD is betting on
AMD.


Who will be the next Unix OEM to work in Tandem with DEC and Sequent?
SKD's
clairvoyant CMOS canine says we'll find out very shortly.




