On 31 Mar 98 13:21:35 EST, dbd@icf4.hrb.com (Douglas B. Dodson) wrote:

>Hi,
>
>I have several DEC Alpha machines running OpenVMS 6.2-1H3 that I would like to 
>be able to connect to using a VT420 through a terminal server.  The Alphas will 
>have their console serial ports connected to the terminal server and then I 
>will run a line from the VT into the terminal server.  I would like to be able 
>to access the Alphas through their console ports whether they are booted or 
>not.  Obviously, if they are not booted, they will not be running LAT.  Can 
>someone give me the steps necessary to set this up?  

You could use reverse-LAT ports.  The Alphas do not need to be booted and
running LAT.  I believe you could set up a service on each of the terminal
server ports and from the VT420, type "C servicename" and it should route you
to the appropriate port on the terminal server.  OR, from a VMS machine
running lat, use LATCP to create LTA ports to each of the Alphas and connect
using a "SET HOST/DTE" command.

-Richard



