A simple way to catch an autoboot before it goes multiuser is to hit ctrl-c
while it is just starting up. Boot the system, and then as the kernel's
device initialization and config stuff gets done running, but right
before you would see 'autoboot in progress' or something, start hitting
^c and it will dorp to the single user prompt. 

you can also circumvent autoboot by manually entering the boot command 
from the chervron, thusly: boot -f 5/rz2/vmunix (that woudl alt least work 
on a 5000/2xx, im not totally sure about a 5000/1xx) 

happy hacking,
