wilson@dbit.com (John Wilson) writes:

>In article <6fsapl$g7@i4got.pechter.org>,
>Bill Pechter <pechter@news.monmouth.com> wrote:
>>RT squared was just a downloadable version of RT11 (I think) that
>>would run memory resident in some PDT's...  I've never seen it.

>I thought I saw something like that in the V4.0 sources named "MRRT-11"
>(memory-resident RT-11).  Are these two different things or am I just
>remembering wrong?

Yes, MRRT was Memory Resident RT.  The execute-only RT which was
available at one point was RT^2 (RT-Squared).  Neither was designed
for the PDT series, though some of the software which was part of
the MRRT effort was designed with TU58s in mind...

In fact, one of the programs was a TU58 emulator which allowed
use of a serial line attached to another machine as if it was a
TU58 drive... it spoke [M]RSP and did just fine at high speeds.
I remember having it working on my 11/10 at home at one point,
though the specific application escapes me at the moment.

					Megan Gentry
					Former RT-11 Developer

