Interesting table, thanks for posting the address. If SGI intends to
stay in the game with the MIPS architecture, they need to do a far
better job articulating their strategy. Of late, all I've heard out of
the firm is the following (extracted from Shannon Knows DEC Volume 5
Number 8, April 2, 1998):

"SGI announced that 48 million MIPS RISC microprocessors were shipped in
1997. This volume makes MIPS the Number One RISC architecture in the
world for the second consecutive year. Moreover, MIPS became the first
RISC architecture to exceed the Motorola 32-bit 68K CISC chip in volume
shipments."

